\section{Middle East}{
Thirteen taxa of bovids, cervids, equids and suids from the Levant, the
Zagros, Syria and Arabia, compiled from:
\itemize{
\item Stewart, M., Louys, J., Price, G. J., Drake, N. A., Groucutt, H. S., &
Petraglia, M. D. (2019). Middle and Late Pleistocene mammal fossils of
Arabia and surrounding regions: implications for biogeography and hominin
dispersals. \emph{Quaternary International}, 515, 12-29.
\item Stiner, M. C. (2005). \emph{The Faunas of Hayonim Cave, Israel}. Peabody
Museum, Harvard.
\item Yeshurun, R., Bar-Oz, G., & Weinstein-Evron, M. (2007). Modern hunting
behavior in the early Middle Paleolithic: faunal remains from Misliya
Cave, Mount Carmel, Israel. \emph{Journal of Human Evolution}, 53, 656-677.
\item Stiner, M. C., Barkai, R., & Gopher, A. (2009). Cooperative hunting and
meat sharing 400-200 kya at Qesem Cave, Israel. \emph{PNAS}, 106,
13207-13212.
\item Tsahar, E., Izhaki, I., Lev-Yadun, S., & Bar-Oz, G. (2009). Distribution
and extinction of ungulates during the Holocene of the southern Levant.
\emph{PLoS ONE}, 4, e5316.
\item Mata-Gonzalez, M., Starkovich, B. M., Zeidi, M., & Conard, N. J. (2023).
Evidence of diverse animal exploitation during the Middle Paleolithic at
Ghar-e Boof (southern Zagros). \emph{Scientific Reports}, 13, 19006.
}

Older names are mapped to current IUCN taxonomy: \emph{Capra ibex} from the
Negev to \emph{Capra nubiana}, and \emph{Ovis orientalis} to \emph{Ovis gmelini}. Fallow
deer are one taxon, \code{Dama_sp}, since \emph{Dama dama} and \emph{D. mesopotamica} are
not reliably separated in the record; the \code{members} column names the two,
which \code{\link[=run_hindcast_series]{run_hindcast_series()}} models separately and then combines. \emph{Equus
ferus}, \emph{E. africanus} and \emph{Gazella arabica} are reported in the sources
but left out on review. Wild boar needs its
own IUCN range polygon alongside the ungulate downloads.

Lists for the other presets are not yet compiled; pass your own species to
\code{\link[=run_hindcast_series]{run_hindcast_series()}} for those regions.
